<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9338] ML TF integration: tf cluster can&apos;t connect after killing first node with default port 10800</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9338</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Case: &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Run cluster with 3 node on 1 host&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Filling caches with data&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Running python script&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Killing lead node with port 10800 with chief + user_script processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;chief and user_script restarted on other node&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;script rerun&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Actual:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;chief and user_secript restarted on other node but started to crash and run again because can&apos;t connect to default 10800 port&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
